omethean-the-created-aa/953932-let-s-cast-them-created?p=953946#post953946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I get how whitewashing works (and I'm not really a fan of it either), but saying cis can't play trans is like saying straight can't play gay or French can't play English. Isn't the whole point of being an actor to play roles?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, casting is a zero sum game. A role that goes to someone else is a role that doesn't go to me, which means I have to find another way to pay my bills until the next role comes along. With my deep voice and prominent Adam's apple, I will never be cast in a role as a cis woman. I just won't. If I were to go on HRT (which I would want to if it wouldn't jeopardize my career), those things wouldn't change. But, I would grow breasts, which would mean I would never be cast in a role as cis man either. That would leave me with trans roles only, which there aren't many of to begin with. As long as those roles are going to cis men, acting will never be a viable career for trans people who don't pass <i>invisibly</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-19-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:37:12-07:00","id":953960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/953932-let-s-cast-them-created?p=953958#post953958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is casting depends so heavily on superficial details. With my deep voice and prominent Adam's apple, I will never be cast in a role as a cis woman. I just won't. If I were to go on HRT (which I would want to if it wouldn't jeopardize my career), those things wouldn't change. But, I would grow breasts, which would mean I would never be cast in a role as cis man either. That would leave me with trans roles only, which there aren't many of to begin with. As long as those roles are going to cis men, acting will never be a viable career for trans people who don't pass <i>invisibly</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense, you have a fair point. I must admit that at first it sounded like &quot;Trans roles to trans people, Cis roles to whoever does it best&quot; and that's what made me react. Thanks for taking the time to explain your point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:Mer